  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Skitgubbe. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Skitgubbe (Swedish: 'Shit Old Man', also known simply as 'Skit' or 'Mattis') is a traditional Swedish card game for 3 players. It is divided into two distinct phases: Phase 1 (Trick-Taking/Collection) where players try to gather good cards, and Phase 2 (Shedding/Battle) where the goal is to get rid of all cards. The loser is the last player holding cards and is declared the 'Skitgubbe'.",
    objective: 'Avoid being the last player with cards in phase 2; the last player left with cards is the loser (the skitgubbe).',
    gameplay: "Two phases. Phase 1: Two-player tricks; player to dealer's left leads, next player plays; higher card wins; no follow suit; after playing, each draws from stock to keep three cards. Equal cards (stunsa): cards stay, both draw, same leader leads again. Option: turn up top card of stock and play it. Last card of stock sets trump for phase 2. Phase 2: Player who drew trump leads; must beat previous card (higher same suit or any trump) or pick it up; trick complete when as many cards as active players; completer leads next or player to left if out.",
    keyRules: [
      'Phase 1: Two-card tricks, higher rank wins, draw from stock after playing.',
      'Phase 2: Beat or pick up; follow suit when beating; trump beats non-trump.',
      'Last card of stock determines trump; holder leads phase 2.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two to four players; best for three.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card pack without joker.',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card pack without joker.',
      dealing: 'Deal three cards to each player clockwise, starting with forehand. Place the remainder face down as the stock (talon).',
    },
    turnFlow: "Two phases. Phase 1: Two-player tricks; player to dealer's left leads, next player plays; higher card wins; no follow suit; after playing, each draws from stock to keep three cards. Equal cards (stunsa): cards stay, both draw, same leader leads again. Option: turn up top card of stock and play it. Last card of stock sets trump for phase 2. Phase 2: Player who drew trump leads; must beat previous card (higher same suit or any trump) or pick it up; trick complete when as many cards as active players; completer leads next or player to left if out.",
